Z||000007||862M4inCA||03-21-2001||08:57 PM||||I've been told that is a problem on most fiero's. The temp guage, when the key is turned to start, jumps all the way to the right (WAY past overheat) basically as a test to verify operation of the guage. The fix I think you are referring to is the one that lights up the temerature light when the key is put to start (like the brake light does). You might try checking the wires from the gauge to the temerature sending unit. On the 4 cyl. it's located on the top left hand side of the head with two wires connected (this is not the ECM connection on the thermostat housing). If you connect the wires to ground with the key on the guage and temp light show an overheat condition (light comes on, temp guage pegs). If that works then I would be suspicious of the sending unit. Hope that helps.||||reg||1
